{
  "$comment": [
    "The physical catalogue: one entry per frame, with the millimetres printed",
    "on a real arm. This file is the single source for frame geometry \u2014 the",
    "artwork generator draws each frame to these dimensions and emits the",
    "matching calibration, and the database seeder reads both back out of the",
    "manifest. Change a measurement here and the picture, the product page and",
    "the try-on all follow; nothing has to be kept in step by hand.",
    "",
    "lensWidthMm and lensHeightMm are boxed dimensions (the bounding box of the",
    "lens aperture), which is the convention the numbers on an arm follow.",
    "totalWidthMm is the full width of the frame front, hinge to hinge \u2014 it is",
    "larger than 2 x lens + bridge by the two end pieces."
